# Setup that works!

- Record player with pre-amp on
- Line reducer, set to ~0.25
- Mic on 43 in alsamixer
- Vol 1 (e.g. don't change volume) in sox

# AirPlay 2
https://github.com/mikebrady/shairport-sync/blob/master/BUILD.md
- Follow Airplay 2 (not classic)

Setting impulse.wav
https://github.com/mikebrady/shairport-sync/wiki/Digital-Signal-Processing-with-Shairport-Sync

# Watchdog
https://diode.io/blog/running-forever-with-the-raspberry-pi-hardware-watchdog

# Record Player
continuously pipe line-in to line-out

systemctl status recordplayer
sudo service recordplayer start

./systemd/system/recordplayer.service

dave@rpi3:~ $ ls -al /etc/systemd/system/multi-user.target.wants/recordplayer.service
lrwxrwxrwx 1 root root 40 Jul 28 19:57 /etc/systemd/system/multi-user.target.wants/recordplayer.service -> /etc/systemd/system/recordplayer.service

# Ensure USB device comes up as same device consistently
# https://discourse.ardour.org/t/sound-card-order-changes-on-boot-up/80915/7
_etc_modprobe.d_alsa-base.conf -> /etc/modprobe.d/alsa-base.conf

aplay -l | grep USB -> should be card 1

------
After a few days, something happens and it starts to hiss.
Seems to be in the USB audio recording step?

Things I tried that didn't help:
- Restarting record-player service
- Reloading audio usb
- Reboot device daily (Wouldn't come back up)

Added /usr/local/bin/shairport-watchdog, with a cron every 10 minutes
- Look for errors pointing at soundcard
- and check soundcard is listed by aplay -l in the right port

And normal watchdog, monitoring network not online

-----

see: /etc/asound.conf

-----

Extra watchdog
- script in /etc/watchdog.d that checks systemd is still responding

------
# Rebuild from scratch (last done 2026-10-05)

Raspberry Pi 3B, Raspberry Pi OS Lite 64-bit (Debian 13 trixie), USB audio = C-Media adapter
(Unitek Y-247A), user `dave` with passwordless sudo.

1. Flash with Raspberry Pi Imager: hostname `rpi3`, user `dave`, ssh with public key.
2. `sudo apt install alsa-utils sox libasound2-plugin-equal nodejs watchdog`
3. Audio: `config/_etc_modprobe.d_alsa-base.conf` -> `/etc/modprobe.d/alsa-base.conf` (USB = card 1),
   `config/asound.conf` -> `/etc/asound.conf`, `config/alsaequal.bin` -> `~/.alsaequal.bin`.
   Mixer (`amixer -c 1`): Mic Capture 20 (~43% in alsamixer), Mic Playback 2, Speaker 30,30;
   then `sudo alsactl store`.
4. AirPlay 2: `./build-airplay2.sh` (deps incl. libplist-utils + systemd-dev, latest nqptp and
   shairport-sync tags, same configure flags as before). Then `config/shairport-sync.conf` ->
   `/etc/shairport-sync.conf`, `sudo usermod -aG www-data shairport-sync`,
   `sudo systemctl enable --now nqptp shairport-sync`.
5. tuneshine: `tuneshine/` -> `~/tuneshine/`; `chmod 711 ~` (trixie homes are 700; shairport-sync
   and www-data need to reach it); `sudo install -o www-data -g www-data -m 664 /dev/null /var/tuneshine-state-request`;
   `config/tuneshine_state_server.service` -> `/etc/systemd/system/`; enable it.
   Check: `curl localhost:8000/playing`.
6. Record player: `config/recordplayer.service` -> `/etc/systemd/system/`; enable it.
7. Watchdogs: `dtparam=watchdog=on` in `/boot/firmware/config.txt`; `config/watchdog.conf` ->
   `/etc/watchdog.conf`, `config/etc_default_watchdog` -> `/etc/default/watchdog`,
   `config/watchdog-systemd-check-copy` -> `/etc/watchdog.d/watchdog-systemd-check`;
   `config/shairport-watchdog-copy` -> `/usr/local/bin/shairport-watchdog`; root crontab from
   `config/root-crontab`; enable `watchdog`.
8. Also in `/boot/firmware/config.txt`: `audio_pwm_mode=2`, `dtoverlay=disable-bt` (Bluetooth unused).

Convolution (`~/impulse.wav`) is off: the old 4.2 build never had it compiled in. `~/rrnoise` was
just a clone of https://gitlab.xiph.org/xiph/rnnoise and isn't used.
